n that they think is great too  much democracy in a way in a way what  ends up coming out of it wouldn't happen  any other way so it's just a matter of  do you like doing it that way or not but  with black hole song specifically  in sound garden i just recorded it in my  basement it's like a bad recording i  played drums played all the instruments  but it's basically what was on the  record just a bad version of it me  playing it all and then give them the  tape and they literally can listen to it  and say  thumbs up thumbs down and that's kind of  where we were at was  if you like it we'll do it if you don't  we won't and what if they'd said to you  they didn't like it that would be enough  to make you leave a band i bet like you  say you know what what do you mean you  don't like this what are you guys the  judging jury no that's where something  like temple of the dog came from where i  was writing songs that i knew weren't  going to be songs that they would like  and uh ended up doing a side project and  that's kind of what side projects are  for sometimes did you write spoon man on  your own yeah spoon man that come to you  like this in your head bam and then you  wrote it down pretty much wow there's a  guy named artist  um the spoon man who's like a seattle  fixture  and he like he could walk in this room  with like his little satchel of spoons  and  and just captivate everyone here oh okay  he's really incredible oh so he must  have been honored when you wrote that  song yeah and he he appeared in the  video and and uh he was great in fact  that was one of the few videos where we  didn't have to be in it it was just  photos of us and then artists going off  and he's fantastic you didn't like the  video aspect of your career i don't  think because you even you even say that  was one of those videos where we didn't  have to be in spoon man which is great  yeah yeah you didn't want to be in that  the black hole sun video i think the  reason why it was so great was because  that was one where i didn't um have any  input and we had just done a bunch of  videos we did one for rusty cage we did  one for jesus christ pose from the from  the same record where  i was basically telling the directors  everything i wanted them to do and it  wasn't it was wasn't coming out good it  was i just didn't like the video so with  black old son i said just find the guy  with a great idea and let him do it and  let the filmmaker make the film i heard  for a while people you hear this every  once more like when bruce springsteen  used to make his videos they say oh  chris cornell's gonna be an actor did  you ever hear that for a while like they  were like  touting you as the next big guy and  acting i had um acting agents trying to  get me to commit to to like letting them  represent me if i decided right and  that's not your thing right they're like  we want to lock you down they use terms  like lock you down  we want to lock you up yeah  in case you decide  i think what they think is if you get a  you know someone sends you a script  whether you're a musician a milkman  whatever you are you're just going to  run and go yes put me in a movie yeah  because everybody wants to be in a movie  did you did you ever consider being a  movie did someone send you screen um i  got a lot of scripts and there's only  one  where i didn't i just said i don't know  anything about this and i don't want to  do it which was the usual suspects and  and uh you could have been in that i  could have been in that and i saw it  took me i saw it like three years later  after it came out and it took me  watching half of it before i even  realized it was the script that they had  sent me

